        },
        "shell": "/bin/launchctl print-disabled system | /usr/bin/grep -c '\"com.apple.screensharing\" => disabled'"
      }
    },
    "default": {
      "additional_info": null,
      "result": {
        "type": "string",
        "value": "PASS"
      },
      "shell": "result=\"FAIL\"\nenabled=$(/bin/launchctl print-disabled system | /usr/bin/grep '\"com.apple.screensharing\" => enabled')\nrunning=$(/bin/launchctl print system/com.apple.screensharing 2>/dev/null)\n\nif [[ -z \"$running\" ]] && [[ -z \"$enabled\" ]]; then\n  result=\"PASS\"\nelif [[ -n \"$running\" ]]; then\n  result=\"${result}  RUNNING\"\nelif [[ -n \"$enabled\" ]]; then\n  result=\"${result}  ENABLED\"\nfi\necho $result"
    }
  },
  "discussion": "Support for both Screen Sharing and Apple Remote Desktop (ARD) is non-essential and _MUST_ be disabled.\n\nThe information system _MUST_ be configured to provide only essential capabilities. Disabling screen sharing and ARD helps prevent the unauthorized connection of devices, the unauthorized transfer of information, and unauthorized tunneling.\n",
  "discussion_format": "asciidoc",
